Since the char is dead, this is for future reference... Arch's are
lawful, Mjollnir is neutral.  There is a chance that you are blasted
by the weapon every time you pick it up, wield it, throw it, etc. 
Mjollnir is not 'intelligent', so the damage is 4d4 if you don't have
magic resistance, 2d4 if you do.

For completeness, intelligent artifacts do 4d10 blasting damage to
non-magic resistant chars, and 2d10 otherwise.

On the other hand, you have an inherent +d5 to hit (+ any enchantment
on the weapon) with Mjollnir and +d24 shock damage to non-shock
resistant monsters.  Of course, later in the game, when you have
ridiculously high str, dex, or both, your inherent bonus to hit will
outweigh the penalty for wielding a restricted weapon (a dex of 18
gives +4, which wipes out the -4 for using an unskilled/restricted
weapon).

